ceres-solver
------------------------------------------
Solving nonlinear least squares problems comes up in a broad range of areas
across science and engineering - from fitting curves in statistics, to
constructing 3D models from photographs in computer vision. Ceres Solver is a
portable C++ library that allows for modeling and solving large complicated
nonlinear least squares problems.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libceres-devel-2.2.0-1bl1
  libceres4-2.2.0-1bl1
  libcholmod5-5.3.0-1
  libgcc1-14.4.0-1
  libglog2-0.7.1-1bl2
  liblapack0-3.12.0-1
  libspqr4-4.3.4-1
  libstdc++6-14.4.0-1
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  eigen3-3.4.0-1
  gcc-g++-14.4.0-1
  libcholmod-devel-5.3.0-1
  libcxsparse-devel-4.4.1-1
  libgflags-devel-2.2.2-1
  libglog-devel-0.7.1-1bl2
  liblapack-devel-3.12.0-1
  libspqr-devel-4.3.4-1
  libsuitesparseconfig-devel-7.8.3-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/ceres-solver/ceres-solver

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/ceres-solver/ceres-solver/archive/refs/tags/2.2.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack ceres-solver-2.2.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./ceres-solver-2.2.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/ceres-solver-2.2.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/ceres-solver-2.2.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libceres4-2.2.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libceres-devel-2.2.0-X.tar.xz

